<Base lang="en" title="Hiring process — TailorMind">
  <h1>Hiring process</h1>
  <p>Five stages. Total ~2–3 weeks. Async-first with two live conversations near the end.</p>

  <h2>Stage 1 — Application review <small>(~2 days)</small></h2>
  <p>You submit the Google Form: CV, LinkedIn, short answers. We screen for fit and read your written reasoning.</p>

  <h2>Stage 2 — Async take-home <small>(window: 5 days, work: 4–6h)</small></h2>
  <p>Deliberately ambiguous spec. We score <em>autonomy</em> (clarifying questions vs documented assumptions), code quality, and <em>criterio</em> (premortem in PR description, decision journal entry, Claude transcript).</p>

  <h2>Stage 3 — Technical interview <small>(90 min, live)</small></h2>
  <p>Pair-coding using Claude. We discuss your take-home and explore one extension.</p>

  <h2>Stage 4 — Criterio interview <small>(60 min, live)</small></h2>
  <p>You bring a <strong>decision journal</strong> of 3 recent work decisions (what / why / expected outcome / confidence %). We walk through them and probe for resulting and hindsight bias.</p>

  <h2>Stage 5 — Culture &amp; offer <small>(45 min)</small></h2>
  <p>Mutual fit conversation, comp, contract, start date.</p>

  <h2>What we measure</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Criterio</strong> — judgment under uncertainty (Kahneman/Klein, Tetlock, Duke).</li>
    <li><strong>Autonomy</strong> — drives ambiguous work to clarity without micromanagement.</li>
    <li><strong>AI fluency</strong> — uses Claude as a force multiplier, not a crutch.</li>
    <li><strong>Engineering rigor</strong> — full-stack quality, tests, docs.</li>
  </ul>
</Base>
